  "primitive": "scrypt",
  "source": "RFC 7914 \u00a712 supplies only the input parameter sets (password/salt) here. AAP-APPROVED DEFERRAL of the RFC 7914 standards-body KAT outputs: HeavyThing bakes the scrypt parameters AND the PRF at COMPILE TIME (scrypt_N=1024, scrypt_r=1, scrypt_p=1, scrypt_sha512=1 => HMAC-SHA512) and IGNORES the runtime N/r/p arguments, whereas RFC 7914 requires runtime-varying N/r/p and an HMAC-SHA256 PRF. Matching the RFC would require modifying read-only HeavyThing source (forbidden by Rule R2 / AAP \u00a70.8.2) or a per-tuple multi-build matrix outside the AAP single-build model (\u00a70.4.1, \u00a70.5.4), so the RFC 7914 expected_hex values are DEFERRED per the AAP deferral policy (\u00a70.10.2 / \u00a70.1.3, the same policy that defers poly1305/chacha20). The expected_hex values below are HeavyThing-actual self-consistency KATs captured from the deterministic reference build (regression anchors); the N/r/p fields are informational only. See tests/harness/kat_scrypt.c header and the Accepted Deviations Registry in tests/README.md for the full deferral record.",
